WEBVTT

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:06.650
<b>GUNDAM
VICTORY
MOBILE SUIT</b>

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:12.610
The furious rain, Makes my heart shake
hageshii ame ga, kokoro wo yuruwaseru

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:15.820
Like it did on that day
Ano hi no youni

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:22.910
But I just ran through, In my dream I had till yesterday
Tada hashirinuketa, kinou made no MY DREAM

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.710
...I still believe
...shinjiteiru no sa

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:34.470
I'm willing to fight, An endless defense
Owari no nai, defense demo ii yo

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:42.350
As long as you, Keep on gazing at me
Kimi ga boku wo, mitsumetsuzukete kureru nara

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:45.270
STAND UP TO THE VICTORY!

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.980
Turn to face all the mornings ahead, And someday
Ikutsumono asa wo mukae, Itsuka kitto

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:53.860
Try to seize them
tsukande miseru

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:56.450
STAND UP TO THE VICTORY!

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:02.120
Even if nothing, Lies on the other side
Sono mukougawa ni, nanimonakutemo

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.040
It doesn't matter to me
kamawanai kara

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:14.050
...Just as long as I can embrace, Your gentle, irreplaceable smile!
Kakegae no nai, kimi no yasashii egao daite

00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:33.830
While Üso and the others were in Arti Gibraltar,

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:39.060
a small Earth Federation Forces unit assisting the League Militaire...

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:44.660
...launched an attack on the Zanscare Imperial Space Fleet.

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:08.600
THE BATTLE OF GIBRALTAR

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:10.430
"The Battle of Gibraltar".

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:10.930
THE BATTLE OF GIBRALTAR

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:17.100
That's right, the Earth Federation Forces attacked us!

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:18.730
At Keilas Guilie?

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:21.230
They call themselves the Bagley Team of the League Militaire,

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:23.630
but since they're using Federation ships,

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:26.900
it's a declaration of war by the Federation upon Zanscare!

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.760
And? What would you have me do, Lt. Pippiniden?

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:32.660
I'm not telling you to do anything.

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:36.260
Just gain control of Arti Gibraltar, Commander.

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:38.360
The Keilas Guilie Fleet...

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:41.500
...is under the direct command of Captain Tassilo Wago.

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:47.260
Yes, and if he wins in geosynchronous orbit, it'll affect your own punishment!

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:48.530
Understood!

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:52.630
Wait! Before that, shouldn't we try and settle this politically?

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:54.660
Commander!

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:59.200
The League Militaire, the Federation, and the PCST are all conspiring.

00:02:59.230 --> 00:03:01.030
There's no room for negotiations.

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:04.760
Is that Tomliat ready to go?

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:08.000
No, we haven't finished its weapons check.

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:10.360
I don't care. It just has to fly.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.230
No, not there!

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:15.260
I said the main nozzle throttle is set too weak!

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:17.130
Sorry! I'll retune it!

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:19.800
You brought a test unit out here?

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:23.500
Yes, Pippiniden sent it. It's called a Memedorza.

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:24.760
Is there a phone around here?

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:26.760
Yeah, in the tent.

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:37.630
Yes?

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:40.560
Oh! It's Katejina, Lieutenant!

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:46.560
We were only able to identify these three BESPA pilots.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:50.760
Have them sent to Zanscare instead of the local forces.

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:51.700
Yes, sir.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.560
She looks beautiful.

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:00.830
Sis?

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:02.000
Yes.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:10.830
A funeral with Yellow Jackets...

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:12.830
Mahalia will probably turn over in her grave.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:16.030
They can all complain about it together in heaven.

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:23.000
Go on now.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:24.100
Right.

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:41.360
Please let me thank her for protecting Üso.

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:43.160
That's thoughtful of you.

00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:44.530
Sorry.

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:45.560
It's okay.

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:51.930
Just dab a little bit on her lips.

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:57.500
I'm envious.

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:58.400
Pardon?

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:02.400
You and Üso will always be together.

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:05.130
Probably even in death...

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:15.930
BESPA again, now?!

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:18.500
Watch what they're doing.

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:25.760
What's going on?

00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:28.430
I'm sending you out into space ahead of me.

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:32.700
I have regular shuttle tickets, so you can leave immediately.

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:35.000
Is it the League Militaire?

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:38.160
Wait at the corporation's satellite in geosynchronous orbit.

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:40.160
A ship will come to get you.

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:42.960
I told them you'll be on the next flight.

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:47.900
I don't want you getting hurt.

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:50.630
Right... And you, Lieutenant?

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:52.360
I'll protect you.

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:55.760
And to do that, I need to stay a bit longer and do something.

00:05:56.530 --> 00:05:57.760
R-Right...

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:10.700
Got it?

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:14.060
The one with beam rotors stopped on top of the building.

00:06:14.530 --> 00:06:16.000
Üso, hurry!

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:19.530
By having a funeral with the Zanscare pilots,

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:22.030
we've preserved our neutrality here.

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:28.760
Leave it to me.

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:31.560
What's he doing here?!

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:33.830
That's a BESPA soldier!

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:39.000
He...

00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:40.000
Wait, Üso!

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:40.900
Why?!

00:06:40.930 --> 00:06:42.330
Something's up.

00:06:42.530 --> 00:06:43.830
Mr. Mandella!

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:45.160
You all look well.

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:50.460
Did you come to claim your pilots' remains?

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:53.360
I appreciate the service you gave them.

00:06:53.530 --> 00:06:57.330
I was hoping to negotiate some way out of this deadlock.

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:00.660
You initiated a mobile suit battle right over us!

00:07:00.700 --> 00:07:02.200
What is there to discuss?!

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:05.830
This is how the Zanscare Forces always act!

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:07.830
Mandella Soone!

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:12.600
I never intended to suppress Arti Gibraltar by force!

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:15.200
Ltjg. Cronicle Asher.

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:19.500
Even if you didn't, the rest of your organization thinks otherwise.

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:22.830
You really don't know where Katejina Loos is?!

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:24.260
No idea!

00:07:27.930 --> 00:07:32.500
I'm sorry, but don't you think he's acting suspicious?

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:39.030
This is the letter Miss Katejina left for you at Kasarelia.

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:57.060
These are images from the observatory?

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:57.860
Yes.

00:07:57.900 --> 00:08:02.500
The so-called Bagley Team is now offering to assist us.

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:05.830
Miss Katejina said she was going to spy for us.

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:10.460
"I think, by staying with the lieutenant,"

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:13.200
"I can get some information and be of use to you all."

00:08:13.230 --> 00:08:15.700
"I want to challenge myself, like you have, Üso."

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:17.200
"Katejina Loos."

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:18.460
There's no doubt about it.

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:22.830
BESPA intend to squeeze Arti Gibraltar from above and below.

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:24.430
So it would seem.

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:28.560
Üso, where are you going?

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:31.200
Just to the shuttle launch area for a bit.

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:32.730
"A bit?"

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:34.500
If you're coming, get on.

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:35.330
May I?

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:36.260
Sure.

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:38.660
What's wrong?

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:42.030
I need to check the shuttle passenger list.

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:43.460
Is this work?

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:44.860
Yeah.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:46.900
Okay.

00:08:58.930 --> 00:08:59.860
Üso!

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:01.300
Miss Katejina!

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:03.830
Üso?

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:07.100
You're going into space?

00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:10.100
Yeah, circumstances have led to this.

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:12.700
There's fighting in space, too!

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:16.500
It's dangerous to go up now! Don't go!

00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:19.200
It's dangerous everywhere.

00:09:19.430 --> 00:09:21.330
Then, I'll go with you!

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:23.930
Look, I have two tickets!

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:25.960
You can't.

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:27.500
Why not?

00:09:28.360 --> 00:09:30.930
Because you're part of their organization now.

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:33.430
They won't just let you leave.

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:37.760
Besides, protecting Shahkti is your mission.

00:09:38.830 --> 00:09:39.600
Well...

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:41.300
You'd leave Shahkti behind?

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:44.930
I have two tickets. Shahkti can come, too!

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:48.160
Üso, I can't go into space!

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:52.800
Mother left me these two tickets so I could help people!

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:53.900
Miss Katejina!

00:09:53.930 --> 00:09:54.560
Here they come!

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:55.930
It's the Yellow Jackets, isn't it?

00:09:55.960 --> 00:09:57.800
Are they bombing us again?

00:09:57.830 --> 00:09:59.100
We're safe in this building!

00:09:59.130 --> 00:10:00.030
You hear that?

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:02.230
Yeah, the sound of the beam rotors.

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:03.930
Will the shuttle leave?

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:06.460
They'd never bomb the mass driver.

00:10:06.630 --> 00:10:07.600
You're right.

00:10:07.630 --> 00:10:10.760
Nothing will affect our route to the satellite.

00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:12.130
Right.

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:17.130
Miss Katejina!

00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:21.960
Goodbye, Üso. I admire your talent!

00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:24.400
Miss Katejina! Wait, please!

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:25.400
Stop!

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:29.360
Miss Katejina!

00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:35.300
They're bombing us! It's the Yellow Jackets!

00:10:35.330 --> 00:10:38.900
Shuttle 1221, activating mass driver! Activating mass driver!

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:41.130
Shahkti? Shahkti!

00:10:46.760 --> 00:10:48.230
Get away from the windows!

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:56.430
Miss Katejina was right. I have to protect Shahkti.

00:10:59.530 --> 00:11:02.700
To those in charge of Arti Gibraltar, I make this demand.

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:06.930
I demand that you surrender to Zanscare at once!

00:11:07.260 --> 00:11:10.500
We've no desire for a meaningless battle.

00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:28.060
Signal from Ltjg. Cronicle.

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:29.430
What is it, Lieutenant?

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:33.530
Commander, we're attacking too soon! Please, pull back!

00:11:33.560 --> 00:11:37.760
If they surrender before Keilas Guilie attacks, it'll look better for me.

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:38.560
But...

00:11:38.600 --> 00:11:41.330
You're not wavering because of that woman, are you?!

00:11:41.360 --> 00:11:42.930
You must be joking!

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:44.430
Enemy unit, ascending!

00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:47.700
Here it comes.

00:11:47.730 --> 00:11:50.360
Lee? He's using the Memedorza?

00:11:53.130 --> 00:11:56.900
Marbet, not one scratch on the mass driver rail!

00:11:58.030 --> 00:11:58.930
Incoming!

00:12:00.630 --> 00:12:02.700
I'll give this thing a combat test!

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:12.460
If we let them get away with this, we'll never be able to face Mahalia!

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:14.100
Mahalia, just wait and see!

00:12:14.130 --> 00:12:16.630
We'll pay them back for you!

00:12:16.660 --> 00:12:19.330
We've got no shortage of opponents, Mahalia!

00:12:29.260 --> 00:12:32.530
Those beams are powerful. A hit at close range would be dangerous.

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:33.700
Mahalia!

00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:36.430
Yeah! We're being bombed!

00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:40.200
Which is why I told you to send a battleship or three this way!

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:44.930
Keilas Guilie is a ship which can attack Earth directly!

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:48.560
In which case, we need to leave for space immediately!

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:52.900
Even if I die here, the corporation won't help either side!

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:55.360
I understand how you feel, but...

00:12:56.300 --> 00:12:58.360
We have to give Oliver and the others some support!

00:12:58.400 --> 00:12:59.830
You're right.

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:11.860
At this point, the League Militaire are practically an army.

00:13:12.260 --> 00:13:14.230
I don't really want to help them anymore.

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:22.600
Odelo! Is the Victory ready?

00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:23.900
What have you been doing?!

00:13:24.160 --> 00:13:25.800
The engines are all warmed up!

00:13:25.960 --> 00:13:27.700
Take care of Shahkti!

00:13:27.730 --> 00:13:28.630
Sure.

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:36.060
I am not going to let anyone else get killed!

00:13:43.660 --> 00:13:45.100
We all have to survive this!

00:13:50.360 --> 00:13:52.160
Don't use your rifle!

00:13:53.360 --> 00:13:55.060
If we score a direct hit here...

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:58.030
...and the enemy mobile suit's main engine explodes,

00:13:58.430 --> 00:14:01.800
it'll wreck the mass driver's rail. Is that why we shouldn't fire?

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:02.800
What?

00:14:05.130 --> 00:14:06.660
Incoming from the sea!

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:10.430
If you stop to think during battle, you die!

00:14:14.930 --> 00:14:17.200
Miss Kite, I'll leave this to you!

00:14:17.230 --> 00:14:18.960
I'll deal with that support unit!

00:14:23.530 --> 00:14:24.360
Incoming!

00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:26.630
Tomliats, forward!

00:14:33.460 --> 00:14:34.360
Behind me?!

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:41.230
Where's the Frying Pan?!

00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:43.760
Why you... Here, of all places?

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:45.400
Shooting, without a care!

00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:49.900
Don't you care about the mass driver rail?!

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:56.260
You people are scum, using the mass driver as a shield!

00:14:56.460 --> 00:14:58.600
I hate people like you!

00:15:07.160 --> 00:15:08.130
Cony!

00:15:11.600 --> 00:15:15.500
Your refusal to shoot an ally is your weakness!

00:15:15.760 --> 00:15:16.800
I have you now!

00:15:18.800 --> 00:15:19.960
A blinder?!

00:15:25.600 --> 00:15:29.230
Amazing! You used the beam saber without blowing it up!

00:15:29.260 --> 00:15:30.330
Thanks.

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:37.100
Why, you... He's good!

00:15:37.400 --> 00:15:41.560
So, you understand the danger of using your rifle here.

00:15:48.730 --> 00:15:50.900
Even if they don't intend to destroy it,

00:15:50.930 --> 00:15:55.960
the rail will eventually be damaged, and Arti Gibraltar itself may disappear.

00:16:00.030 --> 00:16:01.830
It's faster than it looks!

00:16:08.330 --> 00:16:09.830
Getting carried away?

00:16:18.460 --> 00:16:19.500
Damn!

00:16:23.060 --> 00:16:24.930
The mass driver rail!

00:16:31.930 --> 00:16:33.800
I can't let it be destroyed!

00:16:34.100 --> 00:16:36.800
This is a treasure for all mankind!

00:16:36.830 --> 00:16:38.830
You must know that, too!

00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:48.160
That should do it.

00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:51.700
My compliments.

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:55.830
Seeing you defending the rail like this is touching.

00:16:57.860 --> 00:16:59.560
Your suit can stay where it is,

00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:01.530
but the pilot dies.

00:17:01.760 --> 00:17:03.130
Relax.

00:17:03.230 --> 00:17:05.200
One blow, and I'll send you to your rest!

00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:18.060
What? Miss Kite!

00:17:18.560 --> 00:17:20.330
Miss Kite, what happened?!

00:17:24.860 --> 00:17:29.400
Commander, if we keep shooting wildly, we'll hit the mass driver rail!

00:17:29.700 --> 00:17:32.760
We have to shoot that white monster down!

00:17:36.730 --> 00:17:39.800
That's Kite's suit! They got her!

00:17:39.930 --> 00:17:43.100
You and Üso will always be together. Probably even in death.

00:17:43.130 --> 00:17:45.860
I'm jealous. Jealous...

00:17:46.930 --> 00:17:48.500
You!

00:17:53.600 --> 00:17:55.030
That new model!

00:18:01.100 --> 00:18:03.660
Were you were the one who killed Miss Kite?!

00:18:06.030 --> 00:18:09.760
Such spirit! Who the hell is he?!

00:18:16.830 --> 00:18:19.560
Main engine, damaged! We're losing power!

00:18:19.760 --> 00:18:22.500
Commander, please! Launch the escape pod, at once!

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:23.830
Escape?!

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:26.600
Escape...

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:29.430
Enough, Metchet.

00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:31.060
Commander, no!

00:18:36.500 --> 00:18:38.300
I can't lock onto it!

00:18:42.360 --> 00:18:44.430
The Recarl has crash landed?

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:47.100
Commander Fuala! Metchet! Do you read me?!

00:18:52.630 --> 00:18:55.230
Metchet! You should be reading me at this range!

00:18:55.260 --> 00:18:57.500
I'm ejecting Commander Fuala's pod!

00:18:57.700 --> 00:18:59.430
What are you going to do?

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:11.200
A mobile suit on top of the shuttle?

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:12.530
Why?

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:15.130
Miss Katejina is aboard that one!

00:19:19.160 --> 00:19:20.730
I won't let you!

00:19:26.530 --> 00:19:29.630
Why did you have to hold it up, Miss Kite?!

00:19:42.160 --> 00:19:43.360
Please, God!

00:19:43.800 --> 00:19:45.030
Miss Katejina!

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:49.330
Miss Katejina...

00:19:51.430 --> 00:19:55.630
Miss Katejina's gone. Miss Katejina is...

00:19:56.230 --> 00:19:58.130
Cronicle, thank you.

00:19:58.200 --> 00:20:00.100
Right. I'll get you to the airlock, and...

00:20:01.030 --> 00:20:01.930
What?!

00:20:01.960 --> 00:20:02.860
What's wrong?

00:20:02.900 --> 00:20:05.500
Captain, don't get hit!

00:20:05.530 --> 00:20:06.500
I'm trying!

00:20:06.960 --> 00:20:09.230
What if smaller debris comes, too?

00:20:09.400 --> 00:20:10.530
What is it?

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:12.800
Probably an Earth Federation Forces ship...

00:20:12.830 --> 00:20:15.160
...that tangled with Keilas Guilie!

00:20:17.300 --> 00:20:22.700
A Federation Forces ship falling to Earth after a hit by Keilas Guilie, huh?

00:20:33.300 --> 00:20:34.760
Our forces are superior!

00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:38.330
Captain, if you take the shuttle directly to Keilas Guilie,

00:20:38.630 --> 00:20:40.460
nothing bad will happen to you.

00:20:41.060 --> 00:20:44.660
I'm back in space, but still with a string of failures.

00:20:45.160 --> 00:20:49.060
Metchet gave me my life, but what will come of it?

00:20:57.300 --> 00:20:58.330
Kite...

00:21:04.860 --> 00:21:07.430
Üso! You read me? Üso!

00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:09.360
Üso, can you hear me?

00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:12.100
Snap out of it! You're still alive!

00:21:13.600 --> 00:21:18.160
Miss Junko... I... I killed Miss Kite...

00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:24.930
I left her to face the enemy, and she died alone!

00:21:25.430 --> 00:21:27.060
Don't give me that crap!

00:21:27.160 --> 00:21:29.360
Kite was a pro, better than you!

00:21:29.730 --> 00:21:32.360
Any enemy you could beat, Kite could beat, too!

00:21:32.400 --> 00:21:35.330
You're ten years too young to say something that conceited!

00:21:36.730 --> 00:21:38.130
Please don't be angry...

00:21:38.330 --> 00:21:43.060
Miss Junko... I'm sorry. I did my best!

00:21:43.100 --> 00:21:46.700
I know you did, so quit beating yourself up!

00:21:47.860 --> 00:21:50.760
Just cry in there till you feel better!

00:21:51.060 --> 00:21:53.700
Let that be your memorial to her!

00:22:24.060 --> 00:22:29.530
Piercing the sky, Blue lightning
sora wo tsukisasu aoi inazuma

00:22:29.530 --> 00:22:35.320
Staining the earth, With the shadow of greed
daichi o someteku, yokubou no kage

00:22:36.370 --> 00:22:41.460
Once again, when the nightmare, Envelops the Earth
futatabi akumu ga, sekai wo tsutsumu toki

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:46.790
You hear voices crying out "S.O.S."
"SOS" wo sakebu koe ga kikoeru...

00:22:48.630 --> 00:22:54.130
Let proud hope fill your heart
hokoritakaki kibou wo mune ni

00:22:54.720 --> 00:23:03.100
And stand up! Say a prayer for peace!!
tachiagare! heiwa no inori komete!

00:23:04.100 --> 00:23:05.100
WINNERS FOREVER!

00:23:06.100 --> 00:23:08.980
In every age
itsuno jidai mo

00:23:08.980 --> 00:23:14.570
...People take risks for freedom
hito wa jiyuu wo kakete

00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:17.000
WINNERS FOREVER!

00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:21.240
The battle goes on
tatakai tsuzukeru

00:23:21.240 --> 00:23:25.920
Fighting all alone in solitude
kodoku na made ni hitori...

00:23:35.600 --> 00:23:37.860
Üso and the others head into space,

00:23:37.900 --> 00:23:40.230
and encounter an asteroid swarm.

00:23:40.830 --> 00:23:43.000
Amidst the space trash...

00:23:43.600 --> 00:23:48.030
...Üso finds himself standing in front of the gun of a BESPA pilot.

00:23:50.200 --> 00:23:53.260
Next time, on Mobile Suit Victory Gundam:

00:23:53.960 --> 00:23:55.800
Next Episode SPACE DUST
"Space Dust".

00:23:55.800 --> 00:23:56.930
Next Episode SPACE DUST

00:23:56.930 --> 00:23:58.430
Please watch it!
Next Episode SPACE DUST

00:23:58.430 --> 00:23:59.930
Next Episode SPACE DUST
